          "fontSize": 14,
          "text": "Alarippu, traditionally the first piece of a Bharatanatyam Margam. The word 'Alarippu' literally means 'to bloom,' symbolizing the dancer’s journey as they open their body and soul like a flower in offering to the divine, the guru, and the audience.",
